{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Do not come near here.</b> He had not yet attained his great level in prophecy, for at Mount Sinai \"he approached the thick darkness where Elohim was\" (Exodus 20:21). And likewise the matter of the hiding of the face — that he had not yet ascended to what is said of him, \"and he beholds the likeness of YHWH\" (Numbers 12:8)." "<b>For the place on which you stand is holy ground.</b> Even though he was far from the bush, He warned him concerning this, for the entire mountain was sanctified by the descent of the Shekhinah to the top of the mountain, as at the time of the giving of the Torah. And Moses was on the mountain, for there he ascended, as it is said, \"and he came to the mountain of Elohim, to Horeb\" (Exodus 3:1). And the bush was at the top of the mountain, and behold all of it is holy and forbidden for the wearing of sandals. And thus the Sages said: in every place where the Shekhinah is revealed, wearing sandals is forbidden (Shemot Rabbah 2:13), and so too in Joshua (Joshua 5:15), and likewise the priests did not minister in the Temple except barefoot."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:01:33.883218639Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}